## Interpretation

Evidence for order requires all three features:

1. Ordered accuracy rises above chance at an order long enough to cross a `|` number boundary.
2. The independently trained shuffled control remains substantially lower.
3. Applying the ordered model to shuffled held-out sequences destroys its advantage.

If ordered and shuffled controls perform similarly, classification is using digit or exact-number marginals rather than order. If neither works, finite local n-grams up to order 12 do not capture the signal.

This first pass holds out generation seed 13. Any apparent onset order should subsequently be checked with leave-one-generation-seed-out evaluation, especially because selecting the best of twelve orders introduces multiple-comparison risk.